                  Workforce management lies at the heart of every venture. This is because it is the process that deals with the management of employees, data and activities. If we consider any given organization irrespective of the industry, they have multiple departments which implies they have multiple employees as well. This is directly proportional to the fact that the management of the workforce is a complicated affair. This is because keeping a track of the employees, their activity, and the associated data in itself is a very tedious task. Some of the most common challenge in the field of workforce management are as follows:-</p><p>

<h4>1. Time and attendance tracking</h4>
One of the most common issues in workforce management is the aspect of tracking time as well as attendance. This is usually because the tracking is done manually. It is the employee who manually signs in and signs out. This opens a room for inaccuracies and errors. Sometimes the error could be a result of inaccuracy, it can also lead to dishonesty. Further, keeping a track of the entire attendance manually becomes extremely tedious. This has an impact on the overall workforce management hence it also impacts the productivity of the individual.</p><p>

<h4>2. Scheduling and Rostering</h4>
Within the premises of any company from any given industry, there can be several different shift patterns which require the concerned employees to be scheduled for different parts of the day. If we consider the aspect of staff levels,they can be dependent pretty much on the demand of the project. That is considering the busy periods or the periods that are in less demand. Paper based rostering had been increasingly tedious. Even if we consider that the rostering isn't paper based, rostering manually is extremely lengthy and tedious. Further, manual rostering keeps it prone to human error. This has a direct impact on the overall workforce management.</p><p>

<h4>3. Managing absences</h4>
It is the employees that constitute business irrespective of the industry or the size. Therefore, if there are employees planned and unplanned absence of the employees are regular. The aspect of planned and unplanned absence can actually test a business. Unplanned absences can strain any given venture due to the cost of either covering the absence or replacing the employee. Further, unplanned absences definitely have an impact on the holistic production of a venture. Planned absences on the other hand are simpler to deal with. In any case, managing absence is a tedious task more so, if it is manual. This makes workforce management difficult.</p><p>

<h4>4. Self Service</h4>
A crucial aspect of any workforce management is the aspect of employee self service. There is an unprecedented demand on the part of the employees to access their time and attendance information. This is extremely challenging for the employers who are expected to store data in a proper format. The requirement for transparent employee data is challenging. Even if the procedure for storage is digital, it is extremely tough if the process is completely manual in nature.</p><p>

<h4>5. Tracking of Holidays</h4>
It is inevitable, employees of any given venture expect holidays. Some holidays are planned in nature which are relatively easier to deal with. For example, if we consider the aspect of festivities or prescribed holidays. However, unplanned holidays can be considerably tough to be dealt with. It is not possible for the employers to grant holiday requests to a large number of employees at the same time. The provision of holidays constitute an important aspect which is to be accommodated meticulously. Therefore, tracking holidays is important but it becomes extremely tough. Unplanned holidays strain the workforce management inevitably.</p><p>

